  "description": "Executable evidence for ak.vector.mls.cross_station_welcome_replication.v1 (zh/crypto-media/encryption-and-audit.md section 2.2, zh/crypto-media/device-lifecycle.md section 9.2.3, zh/sync/client-sync.md section 10.1, decisions 0119 and 0121). Every governance variant starts from a fresh governance Station. A governance variant has committer author and sign one ak.mls.commit whose inline Adds are exactly the adds endpoints and one producer-signed MlsWelcomeDelivery per added endpoint, sorted by welcome_id; its outcome lists the Welcomes queued on the governance Station, the claims bound there and, per remote committed-replication target, the Welcomes carried by that target's intent (null when the intent carries no welcomes member). A replica variant delivers to Station Y one committed_replication item of item_event_kind carrying the listed Welcomes of that Commit. A Station Y variant that names claims starts from a fresh Station Y whose ledger holds each named claim in the given state (live, absent, expired, consumed, bound_to_other_welcome or other_endpoint); a Station Y variant without claims continues from the state the earlier variants of its case left. queue_capacity and preloaded_deliveries give each endpoint the variant delivers to its queue bound and the unacknowledged deliveries it already holds. queue and claim_bindings list the recipients whose Welcome is queued and whose claim is bound after the variant; outstanding counts unacknowledged deliveries per endpoint. A refused submission or request MUST leave every Station exactly as before.",
